$$
43 + 12 = 55
$$

She finished 44 of these problems at school. To determine how many problems she had left to do for homework, we subtract the number of problems she finished from the total number of problems:

$$
55 - 44 = 11
$$

Thus, the number of problems she had to do for homework is:

$$
\boxed{11}
