First, we need to find out how many files are left after she deleted 40. So, we subtract 40 from 85. That would be 85 minus 40. Let me calculate that. 85 minus 40 is 45. Okay, so she has 45 files left.

Now, she wants to put these 45 files into folders, with each folder holding 5 files. To find out how many folders she needs, we divide the total number of files by the number of files per folder. That means 45 divided by 5. Let me do that calculation. 45 divided by 5 is 9. So, Katie ends up with 9 folders.

